      {
        "id": 171892,
        "name": "Under3",
        "username": "Under3",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/under3/{size}/1872_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-23T09:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don’t really see how the standard basic Sentinels have a chance against Dark Watch. They don’t have the experience to compare to Fixer or Expatriette or the sheer power of the magic of Nightmist (or presumably Harpy).<br>\nWe are comparing here characters who have 4 full decks compared to a team that aren’t strong enough to have their own decks (until void guard). The fluff backs it up too I think, this is one seriously one sided battle. Medico doesn’t have the attacking power, Idealist doesn’t have the defense, Mainstay can tank for a bit but that won’t keep them going for long, and is outclassed in survivability by Setback. Out of all of them Writhe is the most difficult to quantify I think, but that’s then only one man still.<br>\nThe biggest threats to Dark Watch aren’t the Sentinels but are more likely to be Setback or any fall out from Nightmist’s/Harpy’s magic.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:54:41.321Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
